From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:30:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 102/102] ac: CloseAllAsync and GetCloseAllResult

The real NDM calls ac:u 0x0019 CloseAllAsync when it stops its
background connection (right after its CancelConnectAsync), which was
unimplemented. It now ends the caller's own connection and signals the
given event, like CloseAsync; other processes keep theirs, so a running
game isn't cut off (see 0099). 0x001A GetCloseAllResult answers like
GetCloseResult. Both on ac:u and ac:i.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
---
 src/core/hle/service/ac/ac.cpp   | 40 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 src/core/hle/service/ac/ac.h     | 13 +++++++++++
 src/core/hle/service/ac/ac_i.cpp |  2 ++
 src/core/hle/service/ac/ac_u.cpp |  2 ++
 4 files changed, 49 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/core/hle/service/ac/ac.cpp b/src/core/hle/service/ac/ac.cpp
index f51046b5d..9d08dac94 100644
--- a/src/core/hle/service/ac/ac.cpp
+++ b/src/core/hle/service/ac/ac.cpp
@@ -104,23 +104,47 @@ void Module::Interface::CloseAsync(Kernel::HLERequestContext& ctx) {
     // few seconds with the real NDM) signalled the disconnect event of whichever process
     // registered one last and marked everyone offline: Badge Arcade then lost its game server
     // connection right after signing in (006-0114, 2026-10-15).
-    const bool was_connected = ac->connected_processes.erase(pid) > 0;
-    if (was_connected) {
-        if (const auto it = ac->disconnect_events.find(pid);
-            it != ac->disconnect_events.end() && it->second) {
-            it->second->Signal();
-        }
-    }
+    ac->CloseConnection(pid);
 
     if (ac->close_event) {
         ac->close_event->SetName("AC:close_event");
         ac->close_event->Signal();
     }
 
-    ac->ac_connected = !ac->connected_processes.empty();
+    IPC::RequestBuilder rb = rp.MakeBuilder(1, 0);
+    rb.Push(ResultSuccess);
+}
+
+void Module::Interface::CloseAllAsync(Kernel::HLERequestContext& ctx) {
+    IPC::RequestParser rp(ctx);
+    const u32 pid = rp.PopPID();
+    const auto event = rp.PopObject<Kernel::Event>();
+
+    // The real NDM calls this when it stops its background connection (seen 2026-10-16 after its
+    // CancelConnectAsync). On the console the other processes' connections are separate; ending
+    // them here would cut off a running game the way 0099 fixed for CloseAsync, so only the
+    // caller's connection ends.
+    ac->CloseConnection(pid);
+
+    if (event) {
+        event->SetName("AC:close_all_event");
+        event->Signal();
+    }
 
     IPC::RequestBuilder rb = rp.MakeBuilder(1, 0);
     rb.Push(ResultSuccess);
+
+    LOG_DEBUG(Service_AC, "called, pid={}", pid);
+}
+
+void Module::CloseConnection(u32 pid) {
+    if (connected_processes.erase(pid) > 0) {
+        if (const auto it = disconnect_events.find(pid);
+            it != disconnect_events.end() && it->second) {
+            it->second->Signal();
+        }
+    }
+    ac_connected = !connected_processes.empty();
 }
 
